welcome back to the David Pakman show  I'm fairing cousin sitting in for David  Pakman today we need to talk about the  tariffs Donald Trump's trade war may not  be garnering the headlines that it was  when it first began but it is still  there things are still getting bad and  in fact they're actually getting worse  but this week we found out from the US  Department of Agriculture that we the US  taxpayers are about to spend six billion  dollars bailing out the farmers who have  been hurt financially from Trump's trade  wars six billion dollars to fix the bad  policies of Donald Trump now there's an  ulterior motive here and I'm gonna get  to that in just a moment but let's talk  about what's actually happening to these  farmers now we have seen reports ever  since probably about a three to four  weeks after the first tariffs hit  soybean farmers were among the first in  this country to really feel the effects  of it not able to sell their goods  overseas because the prices had gone up  too high because of the retaliatory  tariffs of other countries they end up  with these massive surpluses because of  the surpluses they have to lower their  prices here at home they're not making  as much money we have seen major farms  in the United States laying people off  some saying I'm at the point I'm about  to have to shut down we have obviously  seen you know panels on CNN of farmers  saying uh there's Trump trade wars I was  a trump voter but he did this to me I've  been tricked by the devil and others who  say that I was a trump supporter and I  know he's destroying my farm but I'll  vote for him all over again I'm willing  to die for his trade war that's actually  something a trump supporter said in an  interview I'm willing to die for this  trade war that's a level of crazy I  can't even wrap my head around so let's  move on for a second so we know that the  trade war killing farmers here in the  United States figuratively not literally  and they can't sell their goods so  that's why the USDA has come in and said  all right we're gonna give you this  bailout because Donald Trump said we're  we're gonna spend six billion dollars of  taxpayers money that would be better  spent literally on almost anything else  but we're gonna give it to you and the  farmers have all kind of had the same  response we don't want your handouts we  want the tariffs lifted so that we can  just go back to how things were things  were fine he broke it and you're not  gonna fix it with this little six  billion dollar band-aid that's actually  going to fall off in about six to twelve  months anyway because that's the thing  that people need to understand until the  tariffs are lifted everything we do  whether it's a bailout part of the  bailout also includes the USDA coming in  and buying some of the surplus produce  they're gonna give it to homeless  shelters use it for the military use it  for other things but it's only temporary  I what happens when the next harvest  season comes which we're kind of getting  close to that as well we're gonna have  more surplus is the USDA gonna have to  spend six billion dollars every quarter  just to continuously bail out these  farmers or are we gonna be smart as a  country and get rid of the tariffs that  Trump has put in place because they're  absolutely destroying our economy I  unfortunately believe the answer is  we're gonna keep putting on six billion  dollar band-aids and here's why the  reason this bailout is happening right  now it's not to help the farmers it's to  help the Republican Party that's the  ulterior motive they're not buying  surplus goods they're buying votes  that's what this is about this is a six  billion dollar let's call it an ad buy  for the Republican Party at the expense  of US taxpayers that is our money that's  our money that is being given to them  just to buy their votes for the  Republican Party because as I mentioned  before yeah we have a couple holdouts in  in farm country who say I'll go to the  grave fighting for Trump's trade wars  most of them are not like that most of  them understand that this man doesn't  know what he's doing  the Republicans are complicit with what  he's doing  and this is not a viable policy and it  has to go but if we give them handouts  if we give them you know one hundred two  hundred thousand dollars to keep their  farm going for another six months they  may say okay well I guess I guess this  is okay for now maybe by the time this  money runs out they'll have fix things  and everything will be okay sure I could  vote Republican I guess in the midterms  that is one hundred percent what this is  about this isn't about saving families  this isn't about saving farms this isn't  about buying extra produce and giving it  to homeless people this is about buying  votes to stem the tide of the blue wave  I hope everybody understands that but  part of the blue wave that they're not  going to be able to fix is the fact that  you know there was a retail group  National Retail Federation last week  released a study showing that the  tariffs are going to cost an additional  six billion dollars for US taxpayers  that's in addition to the six billion  we're bailing out it's going to cost us  at an additional six billion dollars in  consumer goods specifically in just the  phirni  furniture and luggage / baggage  industries prices on those goods will  increase for consumers by about six  billion dollars assuming spending levels  stayed the same so we're spending six  billion dollars to give it to the  farmers who are struggling I have  sympathy for them but again they voted  for this guy that they knew wasn't  normal and this is what we could have  all expected but then it's going to cost  us an extra six billion dollars just to  buy a couple different kinds of goods  assuming spending stays the same which  we know it won't once the prices go  sky-high so here's what's going to  happen additionally we're going to see  as prices continue to go up and as we  know wages have fallen and inflation has  already gone up and with the decline in  wages and the rise in inflation our  buying power in the last 12 months has  actually gone down by 3%  now once the  trade war policies start hitting local  stores and everything prices are going  to go up even higher and we're not going  to have the money to buy these things so  sales decline when sales decline they  cut the workforce when the workforce  declines sales decline in other places  because there's fewer people spending  money and so on and so forth as it  ripples through the economy and that is  how economists predict this trade war is  going to help tank things and caused a  major economic collapse Trump doesn't  understand that he wants to bail out the  farmers to buy their votes for the  Republicans for the midterms well who's  going to bail out the furniture industry  who's going to bail out the restaurants  who see their workers or customers not  coming in anymore because they just lost  their job at the furniture company or  furniture factory so they cut ours so  who's gonna bail them out who's gonna  bail out car dealerships when people  can't buy cars anymore because the  prices on those go up we can't just bail  everyone out as what I'm saying we have  to fix the policy that is forcing us to  have to bail people out but to fix it  would have to be for Trump to admit that  he was wrong and that he did this  incorrectly and that'll never happen

